# Keep the architecture diagrams in sync

`docs/excalidraw/*.excalidraw` are generated artefacts. Never hand-edit them —
edit the matching `_generate_*_layer.py` and regenerate.

| Layer | Generator |
|-------|-----------|
| 1 Input | `_generate_input_layer.py` |
| 2 Pre-process | `_generate_preprocess_layer.py` |
| 3 Verification | `_generate_verification_layer.py` |
| 4 Evidence | `_generate_evidence_layer.py` |
| 5 Uncertainty | `_generate_uncertainty_layer.py` |
| 6 Editorial | `_generate_editorial_layer.py` |
| 7 Documentation | `_generate_documentation_layer.py` |

## When to update

Update the affected layer's diagram in the same change as the code whenever you
alter: envelope/payload fields, control flow or branches, enum values, HTTP or
engine behaviour, or which modules a layer calls. Each generator ends with a
"Source of truth" footer listing the files it documents — if you touched one of
those files, the diagram is stale.

## How

```bash
backend\.venv\Scripts\python.exe docs\excalidraw\_generate_input_layer.py
```

Then check the output before finishing:

```bash
backend\.venv\Scripts\python.exe docs\excalidraw\_check.py docs\excalidraw\01-input-layer.excalidraw
```

`_check.py` verifies that every text element fits inside its box, that no
`*-title` wraps, that boxes do not overlap, and that arrows bind to elements
that exist. It exits non-zero on any problem. Prose bodies in `_lib.py` boxes
wrap on purpose, so growing a body means growing the box height and shifting the
rows below it; a wrapping title means the box is too narrow, so widen it.

Still do one thing by hand: grep the generated file for terminology you just
removed.

Boxes use absolute coordinates, so inserting a row means re-spacing everything
below it. Frames are the `f-*` rectangles; keep child boxes fully inside them.

## Thesis framing

Diagram copy follows the same constraint as the code: a failed, blocked,
paywalled, or unsupported fetch is a coverage gap, never a signal of falsity.
Do not add diagram language that implies Layer 1 scores authenticity.
